Shares the WebGPU vertex buffers that hold an attribute's default value. WebGPU
needs a buffer for each attribute a shader declares, so the upload pass bound a
buffer of defaults for each attribute a drawable doesn't provide, and created a
new one each time it rebuilt the drawable's bindings. A symbol drawable
rebuilds them each frame as placement updates its opacities, so every symbol
created buffers each frame, and new bindings reset its pipeline. The context
now keeps one buffer of defaults per attribute type, grown as needed, which
every drawable binds. With the patches before it, the browser demo creates
about 20 buffers a frame while moving instead of 420.
Upstream: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/pull/4938

